commit 8be73636d2e0af4a4fbe50610ce30f83fb785b71 (HEAD)
Author: Seth Junot <xsetech@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Feb 20 03:15:56 2026 -0800

    fix: move getMutableKeys() out of header to prevent dylib ODR violation
    
    The static local variable in the inline getMutableKeys() was duplicated
    across the dylib boundary, causing registerDeviceConfigParserHook() to
    update the test binary's copy while parseArgs() in libc10.dylib checked
    its own separate copy, failing to find device-specific keys.
    
    Moving the definition to AllocatorConfig.cpp ensures a single exported
    symbol with one shared static local, fixing the c10_AllocatorConfig_test
    failure.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

